# E337 draft - task-local Autotools bootstrap closure for OHOS Conan tools

id:                     E443
trigger_tool:           autogen.sh|gettextize|libtoolize|aclocal|automake|glib-genmarshal|glib-mkenums
phase:                  configuration|compilation
error_signature:        (aclocal|automake|libtoolize|glib-genmarshal|glib-mkenums).*Permission denied|gettext source directory .* doesn.t exist|//share/libtool(-conan)?/build-aux|cannot execute.*(aclocal|automake|glib-genmarshal|glib-mkenums)

severity:               3
category:               ohos, autotools, conan, permissions, relocatable
match_keywords:         HMFS, cross-UID, Conan cache, native launcher, gettextize, libtoolize, aclocal, automake, glib-genmarshal, glib-mkenums, relocatable tools
title:                  Build a task-local interpreter and data-path closure for Autotools bootstrap tools on OHOS

root_cause:             An OHOS build task can read scripts from a Conan tool package but HMFS cross-UID policy rejects direct shebang execution. Calling the scripts through Perl, Python, or sh bypasses that executable-file boundary, but Gettext and Libtool scripts can still contain installation-time prefix and data-directory paths that are invalid after Conan package relocation. A working bootstrap therefore needs both an executable interpreter bridge and task-local relocation of the scripts' data paths.
affected_scope:         Conan recipes that bootstrap an Autotools source archive on an OHOS worker and consume packaged Automake, Gettext, Libtool, or GLib code-generator scripts from a cache materialized by another UID or at another Conan home.
verification_cmd:       Run a fresh single-package shadow CI build, require autogen.sh and configure to finish, run the upstream make check, run test_package, and verify that the shared dependency package directories were not modified.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           task-local-native-interpreter-and-relocation-closure
rec_description:        Copy only the required scripts below the current build folder; patch copied Gettext and Libtool prefix/data paths to their resolved Conan package folders; expose readable shell text when upstream reads a tool with sed; otherwise place a small native launcher at the literal command name that execs a fixed system interpreter with the copied script and required data-directory arguments. Put the task-local tool directories first in PATH and set supported variables such as ACLOCAL, AUTOMAKE, GETTEXTIZE, LIBTOOLIZE, gettext_datadir, ACLOCAL_PATH, and PKG_CONFIG_PATH.
rec_command:            CI_PACKAGES="archives/a/avahi-glib/0.9_rc5" zsh ci/conan/build_and_test.sh
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-recipe

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      explicit-interpreter-tool-overrides
fallback_description:   When the upstream build accepts complete tool commands, point its tool variables directly at a fixed interpreter plus the packaged script and explicit data directories. Use the native launcher form when the build invokes a literal command name or cannot preserve a multi-word override.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          conan-recipe

forbid_1_pattern:       chmod.*\.conan2|sed -i.*\.conan2|replace.*package_folder
forbid_1_reason:        Permission bits and embedded paths in a shared Conan cache are not task-owned mutable state, and chmod does not remove the cross-UID HMFS execution boundary.
forbid_1_consequence:   Builds become order-dependent, can corrupt other jobs, and may still fail with Permission denied.
forbid_2_pattern:       hardcode.*/storage/Users/.*/\.conan2|copy.*gettextize.*native launcher
forbid_2_reason:        A developer-specific Conan home is not relocatable. Some upstream bootstrap scripts read the gettextize file as shell text, so replacing that command with an ELF launcher breaks the caller even though direct execution would work.
forbid_2_consequence:   The recipe succeeds only in one cache layout or fails when sed reads an ELF file instead of the expected shell program.

principles:             P013,P014
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             E209,E228,E260
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

